2026-09-28 — shared return and fixed-prototype conversion constraints

The old compiler accepts all 20 invalid written forms in parse-only mode:
11 return cases and 9 direct/indirect fixed-argument cases. This includes dead
branches, incompatible pointed-to/record/function types, nested qualifiers,
array extents and non-null implicit integer/pointer conversion. A non-void
bare return also reached E3101 on emission instead of a frontend refusal.
EvoIR Section 10.1.18 already requires E2202 for incompatible implicit pointer
conversions at these sites; this repairs enforcement, not a new cast prohibition.

GREEN: reuse simple-assignment compatibility before numeric conversion and
after transparent-union argument selection. Invalid value types use E2202;
bare/void/value return mismatches use the newly unused E1207. E1205 and E1206
keep their existing meanings. All 80 negative compiler-mode observations
(20 programs x parse/C-HIR/EvoIR/assembly) reject before output. The old frozen
compiler remains unchanged and confirms 20/20 parse-only false acceptances.

Positive controls preserve GNU sign/immediate qualification/function-void
conversions, explicit casts, arithmetic, aggregate/vector values, old-style
default promotion and once-only side effects. The full affected regression
initially exposed missing va_list record compatibility and __int128 pointer
type inference; both shared rules are repaired. Valid full-width add/subtract,
compound updates and null conditionals pass, while existing overflowing VLA
index tests still report E3011. A by-value va_list copy preserves the caller's
position. Recovered partial ASTs after a parser error are not a legal lowering
input; the old late-refusal test now asserts the earlier E1207 diagnostic.

Validation:
  - Four CLI tests exercise all four modes; both positive interpreters exit 0.
  - 123 targeted CLI/parser/lowering tests pass, including VLA and varargs.
  - 80 GCC14/Clang19 x O0/O2 negative controls reject with explicit -Werror.
    This does not assert that default GCC rejects every GNU extension.
  - 12 legal native executions (two sources x three compilers x O0/O2) exit 0.
  - Ten unchanged original musl commands emit identical assembly to their
    earlier controls and assemble; their installed object hashes do not change.
  - All 1,339 original musl sources pass a 56-second read-only parser sweep.
    No object is assembled or installed by that sweep. Existing diagnostic
    omissions remain disclosed; floating-complex/native/library acceptance
    does not follow from parsing those source files.
  - The final ten-crate gate passes 2,362 tests, zero failures and four
    historical ignored tests; Clippy -D warnings and workspace fmt pass.

Preserved unsuccessful attempts: the first complete gate exposed seven
regressions, not PASS; the first native positive fixture lacked an out-of-line
definition for its old-style control and failed to link. The final fixture
defines and actually executes that control with float-to-double promotion.
Neither failure is concealed as a successful compiler or native run.

